[{:db/id "q-17551/selection/ba488c79319a4de6f796096d70d9741cf9aa81dfb98630c20921c94c3fa19bf2" :answer/id #uuid "c7bd08ab-6219-5ad0-a2d6-a92d69ad1133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17551/selection/d8d9c5d6ea7de2690b493802e3ea12f2a2ec2c9642e45075a162a4226ac30046" :answer/id #uuid "30b99783-ce7f-5eb5-a672-1e848a833cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17551/selection/ab2823d2b1cb9151119c9f0c6fac636a60d0429a052c0dedd6be025ee71073c9" :answer/id #uuid "ba53dd54-19d5-505c-a366-c7a60eb92959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17551/selection/0f094bd64fb361999d825e18a413b1dd7d50b8a2d9a822ef58b3b532148c39ce" :answer/id #uuid "d3905785-3b09-5f49-9940-f2e1b6c801f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17551/selection/38b061a80b50da33c9aa09e8692663e9efea8aac8159d4208ddfbc7d4282f566" :answer/id #uuid "031b7a68-a1aa-55a6-885e-86921ecd9dc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17551/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15833779-4f0a-53bf-b413-2b5429b14500" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17551/selection/ab2823d2b1cb9151119c9f0c6fac636a60d0429a052c0dedd6be025ee71073c9" :answer-field/choices ["q-17551/selection/ba488c79319a4de6f796096d70d9741cf9aa81dfb98630c20921c94c3fa19bf2" "q-17551/selection/d8d9c5d6ea7de2690b493802e3ea12f2a2ec2c9642e45075a162a4226ac30046" "q-17551/selection/ab2823d2b1cb9151119c9f0c6fac636a60d0429a052c0dedd6be025ee71073c9" "q-17551/selection/0f094bd64fb361999d825e18a413b1dd7d50b8a2d9a822ef58b3b532148c39ce" "q-17551/selection/38b061a80b50da33c9aa09e8692663e9efea8aac8159d4208ddfbc7d4282f566"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17551" :question/id #uuid "c4e0ff01-0168-5a21-86ae-f3bb3a7c014f" :question/math-academy-id "q-17551" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ can be used to transform the equation \n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ with the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{z}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-{z}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}) & ={z}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{z}^{-1} \\\\ -x{z}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={z}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{z}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x).\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{1}{x}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-\\frac{1}{x}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17551/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5238ea-c44b-54dd-829b-0da094fb43e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191/selection/07efa0ff5885fb59a7cb0366c3e2a5cfad30a1520a95421db8c53a8b2e583777" :answer/id #uuid "523691f3-2429-5fb3-99a6-10d3275f1676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191/selection/0f094bd64fb361999d825e18a413b1dd7d50b8a2d9a822ef58b3b532148c39ce" :answer/id #uuid "2bf02f9d-5004-54d6-be71-ebcedb407785" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191/selection/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" :answer/id #uuid "89c55c94-8638-527f-a9ac-d282a8f7693b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191/selection/692739b021e243b5d1f52077e7ed9ffd7bc5cec43704d9fc8375ec4409c9ff6c" :answer/id #uuid "9a859bcb-8248-50e2-8af4-3ac2f99488b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191/selection/39df1e289bcd737ec28eb793e91a13b2832f80f4efc359f03b3c5e44f095b32b" :answer/id #uuid "9ec0b724-e7db-5c33-b456-8f624983aff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c221a919-d28e-54df-be96-6278aa6fc0ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-167191/selection/07efa0ff5885fb59a7cb0366c3e2a5cfad30a1520a95421db8c53a8b2e583777" :answer-field/choices ["q-167191/selection/07efa0ff5885fb59a7cb0366c3e2a5cfad30a1520a95421db8c53a8b2e583777" "q-167191/selection/0f094bd64fb361999d825e18a413b1dd7d50b8a2d9a822ef58b3b532148c39ce" "q-167191/selection/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" "q-167191/selection/692739b021e243b5d1f52077e7ed9ffd7bc5cec43704d9fc8375ec4409c9ff6c" "q-167191/selection/39df1e289bcd737ec28eb793e91a13b2832f80f4efc359f03b3c5e44f095b32b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167191" :question/id #uuid "ede66293-c689-51a4-9dc6-fabe30116735" :question/math-academy-id "q-167191" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{3}$ can be used to transform the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}-{x}^{2}y\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{1/3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3{z}^{2/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{3{z}^{2/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{z}^{2/3}}-{x}^{2}{z}^{1/3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3{x}^{2}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x).\n$$\n\nDoing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3{x}^{2}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}z & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=3{x}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-167191/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5238ea-c44b-54dd-829b-0da094fb43e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167191"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553/selection/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer/id #uuid "61c71055-ce6d-5f28-bbb3-87292c96fd8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553/selection/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "077a02d6-e7eb-5a7c-94ad-3bcd5f8f7ce1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553/selection/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" :answer/id #uuid "9d274ef6-83ea-54d2-b982-47b9de099b54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553/selection/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer/id #uuid "6a69b20a-2e80-51f8-b661-8387983a9807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553/selection/1c6961163813a6e3b69ac0678fca4dc3447354e3e0240bbb5bdb5209e1893021" :answer/id #uuid "bea5b25d-0561-578a-9980-3e9a2403eac6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cc039ab-274f-5b80-a3f1-c01a19ce4425" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17553/selection/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer-field/choices ["q-17553/selection/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" "q-17553/selection/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" "q-17553/selection/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" "q-17553/selection/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" "q-17553/selection/1c6961163813a6e3b69ac0678fca4dc3447354e3e0240bbb5bdb5209e1893021"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17553" :question/id #uuid "9be9d070-ba95-553b-81f6-1e94972f6f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-17553" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ can be used to transform the equation \n\n$$\n-x\\frac{dy}{dx}={y}^{2}-y\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ with the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{z}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x(-{z}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}) & ={z}^{-2}-{z}^{-1} \\\\ x{z}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={z}^{-2}-{z}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x).\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{x}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17553/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5238ea-c44b-54dd-829b-0da094fb43e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "37b095fc-798e-55b6-af99-405fb2f6773a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768/selection/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer/id #uuid "7509822b-c0e6-59c6-877b-6854eea650d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768/selection/ab2823d2b1cb9151119c9f0c6fac636a60d0429a052c0dedd6be025ee71073c9" :answer/id #uuid "765b382b-bfc1-55fe-bf9d-1d45f9804b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c0ea6438-d2a9-5bb4-81a1-103242fb27fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768/selection/d57993aeadfb1b8cbcab1a8347876bf0c676c08f01ebc4c064f1c361cda26f51" :answer/id #uuid "6c148c40-f13e-5318-b25c-f3015a894b31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba4bb4b6-93c7-5a97-9f9c-f216c871bf67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79768/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-79768/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-79768/selection/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" "q-79768/selection/ab2823d2b1cb9151119c9f0c6fac636a60d0429a052c0dedd6be025ee71073c9" "q-79768/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-79768/selection/d57993aeadfb1b8cbcab1a8347876bf0c676c08f01ebc4c064f1c361cda26f51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79768" :question/id #uuid "87924d0a-6b63-5a30-a55c-848153ca642c" :question/math-academy-id "q-79768" :question/problem "The substitution $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ can be used to transform the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=xy\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{z}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{z}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z{e}^{z}=x{e}^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x).\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{z}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z) & =x{e}^{z} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79768/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5238ea-c44b-54dd-829b-0da094fb43e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79768"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602/selection/a2c68c3ccde9afd7df4007eb5c1ca8e915b21b6540ad4537bdc5797fa761c8b4" :answer/id #uuid "07bc72ff-3119-5d8a-aeb3-d8a695c020b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602/selection/d36e5a05d5b5e04536a4916a55b1214e26df522de06f95aab619d0950aea715d" :answer/id #uuid "c2deb9fb-22aa-5920-b3ff-263429d6de31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602/selection/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" :answer/id #uuid "e943a725-23ee-5053-b45c-13a7f58ececb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602/selection/243edc54dad7755d0753d38a589add34d7c9d01e89115dbe19945f670c34fd57" :answer/id #uuid "a7737f8a-b73e-535b-9df0-2c4ec415a4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602/selection/19a5fb4833b1ef43c3b64e0fcb5e0403aff2eda01e7701bb61e3d2699cb4cb6e" :answer/id #uuid "980448dd-a1e8-52fe-8a83-3190fe1a5a5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26cf94f0-228e-5db2-88bc-4f177ca42b46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-166602/selection/19a5fb4833b1ef43c3b64e0fcb5e0403aff2eda01e7701bb61e3d2699cb4cb6e" :answer-field/choices ["q-166602/selection/a2c68c3ccde9afd7df4007eb5c1ca8e915b21b6540ad4537bdc5797fa761c8b4" "q-166602/selection/d36e5a05d5b5e04536a4916a55b1214e26df522de06f95aab619d0950aea715d" "q-166602/selection/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" "q-166602/selection/243edc54dad7755d0753d38a589add34d7c9d01e89115dbe19945f670c34fd57" "q-166602/selection/19a5fb4833b1ef43c3b64e0fcb5e0403aff2eda01e7701bb61e3d2699cb4cb6e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166602" :question/id #uuid "41db09fd-a700-5724-9a0d-5294d6c6c5f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-166602" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{-3}$ can be used to transform the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-3}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1/3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-3{y}^{-4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{3{z}^{4/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3{z}^{4/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{4/3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{z}^{1/3}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x).\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-166602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5238ea-c44b-54dd-829b-0da094fb43e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-166602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789/selection/9beddb7036cc94b021caf0f661afba211e5dbe5f321d0915d5e2dc6192494e0d" :answer/id #uuid "862d78a5-8f73-5469-89fc-dd0d6d8a22e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789/selection/c6584f0d9d811c42018930e2f74869e81053f748e38c01f469a52119233531ff" :answer/id #uuid "3cbae2f8-af8f-5b4f-8600-7200f90ef4fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789/selection/2bedfe97ac29471c846e7bb3aab719abe4ad473467c03be0f8454b740cf2146f" :answer/id #uuid "ee42f2f5-e282-5965-bd35-f258bd9e6cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789/selection/d51017e9ad79f46e8fee1a3b581e99ba7418fa24a70c036c13c9f276e701420e" :answer/id #uuid "0116a6b5-691c-5673-88e9-9a74d48e4b3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{C{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789/selection/4d083d651d6b632b14effb9f2b895d8ce7dc408ce8f0a39cbc78f035291dddd3" :answer/id #uuid "d3197f32-b486-583b-816c-81ba3302a94f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{x+\\frac{C}{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80534cbf-bee4-51e0-bab1-cd3adda8f948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79789/selection/c6584f0d9d811c42018930e2f74869e81053f748e38c01f469a52119233531ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-79789/selection/9beddb7036cc94b021caf0f661afba211e5dbe5f321d0915d5e2dc6192494e0d" "q-79789/selection/c6584f0d9d811c42018930e2f74869e81053f748e38c01f469a52119233531ff" "q-79789/selection/2bedfe97ac29471c846e7bb3aab719abe4ad473467c03be0f8454b740cf2146f" "q-79789/selection/d51017e9ad79f46e8fee1a3b581e99ba7418fa24a70c036c13c9f276e701420e" "q-79789/selection/4d083d651d6b632b14effb9f2b895d8ce7dc408ce8f0a39cbc78f035291dddd3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79789" :question/id #uuid "c298cadd-7f69-5fcf-9794-fefcf1b16d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79789" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{y}\\,,\\,y>0\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y={(z+{x}^{2})}^{1/2}\\,.\n$$\n\n]\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2(z+{x}^{2})^{1/2}}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2x).\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2(z+{x}^{2})^{1/2}}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2x)+(z+{x}^{2})^{1/2} & =\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(z+{x}^{2})^{1/2}} \\\\ x(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2x)+2(z+{x}^{2}) & =8{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2x+\\frac{2}{x}(z+{x}^{2}) & =8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}z & =4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/x\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\,z) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 4x \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2xz & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}z) & =4{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {x}^{2}z & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79789/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8dc2b61-3e0a-5e73-83df-04cc621d5feb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79789"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784/selection/26c9b1ed7b376fe34816c6a3880800e47808ccf8516bbaa56bf1d28865686ab2" :answer/id #uuid "c89f714a-4666-543d-8aa9-d057e010b3ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{8}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784/selection/ed635096249118bd18e5a5d45358ddb2e141e3742a8681a3fd75f2306cdc8ef6" :answer/id #uuid "61cee789-c46f-598b-8034-47dd37de7300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{8}+C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784/selection/9f491564f4ce373b0b146c9413b4443921ca3fb636a29cb31b5c80a9db028f48" :answer/id #uuid "ce0d507a-6d13-5eb5-a033-da5f9c0e7591" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784/selection/4a7acfafd0b9f0f2dbab178f865a6241d094b2cdcfece879a2ad00457ccce746" :answer/id #uuid "f6d624d9-b2be-53ef-ad07-6c197e1acc71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784/selection/1d75ba019351bf7140fe4fa791be5b7072caad4cbb36332da4400a517f7f7fc7" :answer/id #uuid "91dc1fe2-9769-56ae-b9fb-1d256c10d065" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{({x}^{4}+C)^{2}}{{x}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3eff7c0-eef4-5559-84d8-9476c4d5c9f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79784/selection/1d75ba019351bf7140fe4fa791be5b7072caad4cbb36332da4400a517f7f7fc7" :answer-field/choices ["q-79784/selection/26c9b1ed7b376fe34816c6a3880800e47808ccf8516bbaa56bf1d28865686ab2" "q-79784/selection/ed635096249118bd18e5a5d45358ddb2e141e3742a8681a3fd75f2306cdc8ef6" "q-79784/selection/9f491564f4ce373b0b146c9413b4443921ca3fb636a29cb31b5c80a9db028f48" "q-79784/selection/4a7acfafd0b9f0f2dbab178f865a6241d094b2cdcfece879a2ad00457ccce746" "q-79784/selection/1d75ba019351bf7140fe4fa791be5b7072caad4cbb36332da4400a517f7f7fc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79784" :question/id #uuid "144b4980-16bd-56a0-bd2d-6e2904dde295" :question/math-academy-id "q-79784" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8x{y}^{1/2}-\\frac{4}{x}y\\,,\\,y>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{1/2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1/2}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}=\\frac{1}{2{y}^{1/2}}\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}=2z\\frac{dz}{dx}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =8xz-\\frac{4}{x}{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =4x-\\frac{2}{x}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =4x-\\frac{2}{x}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}z & =4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}z) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (4x) \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2xz & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}z) & =4{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {x}^{2}z & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{{x}^{4}+C}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{{x}^{4}+C}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\frac{({x}^{4}+C)^{2}}{{x}^{4}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79784/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8dc2b61-3e0a-5e73-83df-04cc621d5feb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-17546"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\n2(1+{x}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}-2xy\\,,\\,y>0\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{1/2}\\,.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $y(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2{z}^{1/2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1+{x}^{2})}{{z}^{1/2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{1/2}}-2x{z}^{1/2} \\\\ (1+{x}^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1-2xz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+{x}^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1-2xz \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2xz}{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,z & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2x/(1+{x}^{2})dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =1+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=1+{x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+{x}^{2})\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,z) & =(1+{x}^{2})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\ (1+{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2xz & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[z(1+{x}^{2})] & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[z(1+{x}^{2})]\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z(1+{x}^{2}) & =x+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{x+C}{1+{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{x+C}{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{\\frac{x+C}{1+{x}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere in the last step we used that $y>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-17544"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y+2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{x}\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1}\\,\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{z}^{-1}+2{x}^{2}{z}^{-2}}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{xz}+\\frac{2x}{{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{z}{x}-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{z}{x}-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-2x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-2x) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-2{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int 2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{3}}{3x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{3}}{3x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x}{C-2{x}^{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552/selection/19a7cbf19b9496f32af9454f8562e67bf763c4327c535e2e16c40d2d57db72df" :answer/id #uuid "6f19dadc-9a47-59fe-8d57-14ca9a0f095a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552/selection/9095a45a2d49ee9b779a743a47be2834c5443067d2d32a285301711841625994" :answer/id #uuid "f814935a-3005-55a2-aacc-7b2a0929f3ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552/selection/78b39e66075e61a1a68bf5dd670b69e148d0af172e8c4d668f68b4630985096b" :answer/id #uuid "59ca6c49-6b6b-5efa-9d96-1f6004f090cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{-1}{1+C{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552/selection/c6a065bc1376493f98e83101ce61404a8dd9338c0c3f5fb0a7e324dc6e2773dc" :answer/id #uuid "197b642a-007d-568a-ab5d-e44698445089" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{-1+C{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552/selection/c68b6d792f0434940bb8f6f67cfc0203e5be5263899b6fdd7f94966d1abb1292" :answer/id #uuid "58d16a85-9e04-5f05-b7d5-8cf620b3a60b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{-1+Cx}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98047d80-b5b5-5e6e-82bb-eb5ebd0f6a0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17552/selection/19a7cbf19b9496f32af9454f8562e67bf763c4327c535e2e16c40d2d57db72df" :answer-field/choices ["q-17552/selection/19a7cbf19b9496f32af9454f8562e67bf763c4327c535e2e16c40d2d57db72df" "q-17552/selection/9095a45a2d49ee9b779a743a47be2834c5443067d2d32a285301711841625994" "q-17552/selection/78b39e66075e61a1a68bf5dd670b69e148d0af172e8c4d668f68b4630985096b" "q-17552/selection/c6a065bc1376493f98e83101ce61404a8dd9338c0c3f5fb0a7e324dc6e2773dc" "q-17552/selection/c68b6d792f0434940bb8f6f67cfc0203e5be5263899b6fdd7f94966d1abb1292"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17552" :question/id #uuid "23f7cb90-301b-5baf-815d-3ddcf267e164" :question/math-academy-id "q-17552" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}={y}^{2}-y\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution* $z={y}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1}\\,\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{z} \\\\ -\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-1+z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-z & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-1,\\,Q(x)=-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-x}$ yields:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}\\cdot (\\frac{dz}{dx}-z) & ={e}^{-x}\\cdot (-1) \\\\ {e}^{-x}\\frac{dz}{dx}-{e}^{-x}z & =-{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\frac{d}{dx}(z{e}^{-x}) & =-{e}^{-x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(z{e}^{-x})\\,dx\\, & =-\\int {e}^{-x}\\,dx \\\\ z{e}^{-x} & ={e}^{-x}+C \\\\ z & =1+C{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =1+C{e}^{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{x}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17552/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8dc2b61-3e0a-5e73-83df-04cc621d5feb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138/selection/3f7fad48c716b2403de39ec72e72e1d9ecd41ac29f5cffb2b27444c1b6ee8214" :answer/id #uuid "228e5c2b-6ce2-5c61-9542-d89ef79b4acd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{6}}{{x}^{5}+7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138/selection/eb4e34222464859884eba6c96a8f8559de8d1cf6ec7aa978c374bc97654d1db6" :answer/id #uuid "d6a68ba3-389b-56f9-8a81-670c1faa10db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt[3]{9-{x}^{5}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138/selection/eb29443707830afe71c2b5f84b969d48516f647126f42a9b0588c2e597395c74" :answer/id #uuid "fd7857b4-3f32-50c2-a3d4-ecaf266eee97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5{x}^{6}}{49-9{x}^{5}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138/selection/fae521994a5fded9349295ca79b29318d535cf85a34134a91c2533ab05a9d445" :answer/id #uuid "9e3779e0-43b3-5103-a182-af8d9e9b39d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{3x}{25{x}^{3}-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138/selection/d5481804a68500fb7107826b5b9f6b14ce35e67372fe002e8c68281e58289027" :answer/id #uuid "f4f47906-baa1-5ae8-946d-6b0b0dc74380" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{12-4{x}^{5}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4045b50-24b1-5218-a922-c4df6b60b9c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-168138/selection/eb29443707830afe71c2b5f84b969d48516f647126f42a9b0588c2e597395c74" :answer-field/choices ["q-168138/selection/3f7fad48c716b2403de39ec72e72e1d9ecd41ac29f5cffb2b27444c1b6ee8214" "q-168138/selection/eb4e34222464859884eba6c96a8f8559de8d1cf6ec7aa978c374bc97654d1db6" "q-168138/selection/eb29443707830afe71c2b5f84b969d48516f647126f42a9b0588c2e597395c74" "q-168138/selection/fae521994a5fded9349295ca79b29318d535cf85a34134a91c2533ab05a9d445" "q-168138/selection/d5481804a68500fb7107826b5b9f6b14ce35e67372fe002e8c68281e58289027"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168138" :question/id #uuid "f4e760df-f892-5b96-a244-f56ee5aadc9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-168138" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}=3{y}^{4}+2xy,\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}\\,z=-\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{-3}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-3}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}z=-\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{6}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 6/x\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{6}} \\\\  & ={x}^{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{6}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}\\,z) & ={x}^{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\ {x}^{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+6{x}^{5}z & =-9{x}^{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{x}^{6}z] & =-9{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{x}^{6}z]\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -9{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {x}^{6}z & =-\\frac{9}{5}{x}^{5}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-9{x}^{5}}{5{x}^{6}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=5{C}_{1}.$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-3}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-3} & =\\frac{C-9{x}^{5}}{5{x}^{6}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =\\frac{5{x}^{6}}{C-9{x}^{5}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5{x}^{6}}{C-9{x}^{5}}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the initial condition  $y(1)=\\frac{1}{2}$ we determine $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5}{C-9}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8} & =\\frac{5}{C-9} \\\\ C-9 & =40 \\\\ C & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5{x}^{6}}{49-9{x}^{5}}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-168138/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e10cdc0-93c4-5b49-8eae-975665bb1d09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556/selection/1f50b516246c9eec4e6aa0d5b1f287ba46735c361cd3fc15d9d1bb891b1b98bf" :answer/id #uuid "794bbd1e-839d-5b78-b753-947aeb8ccfd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{5-2{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556/selection/7cdd51955c22b0409896370980a73c8e7f80a78c2673ef1cc2fca938140e8484" :answer/id #uuid "e5585058-dc0b-58ed-a241-b9b183f0aeac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556/selection/c38685b20b66ffa2d88896bc0ca79a9591024a4d8a6492618cb5b06452e2c80a" :answer/id #uuid "ac31b18e-0d95-5b66-a596-f77104167ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2x}{3-2{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556/selection/99c3d2e3b0698a0e9cd6e4181fa00bff2dac769330ecdd0bb355de8c3608b85c" :answer/id #uuid "f5d53181-c9c4-50dc-b262-3e768d905f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2x}{2-{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556/selection/4a92baaa5b4fb7f5bbbc54aac2fe2249eefce9ecf61cbd527793ac6db78a36b2" :answer/id #uuid "8b6ba78f-0d0e-524f-ad14-b8fe74fe792c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{6x}{5-2{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f515bcb-e83a-5dab-ac90-15603499b35e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17556/selection/4a92baaa5b4fb7f5bbbc54aac2fe2249eefce9ecf61cbd527793ac6db78a36b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-17556/selection/1f50b516246c9eec4e6aa0d5b1f287ba46735c361cd3fc15d9d1bb891b1b98bf" "q-17556/selection/7cdd51955c22b0409896370980a73c8e7f80a78c2673ef1cc2fca938140e8484" "q-17556/selection/c38685b20b66ffa2d88896bc0ca79a9591024a4d8a6492618cb5b06452e2c80a" "q-17556/selection/99c3d2e3b0698a0e9cd6e4181fa00bff2dac769330ecdd0bb355de8c3608b85c" "q-17556/selection/4a92baaa5b4fb7f5bbbc54aac2fe2249eefce9ecf61cbd527793ac6db78a36b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17556" :question/id #uuid "d5c02985-b98e-5a6d-903a-448a7295c82b" :question/math-academy-id "q-17556" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y}{x}+x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=2,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation*\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-x\n$$\n\n*using the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-x.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-x) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{dz}{dx}+z & =-{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{d}{dx}(xz) & =-{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(xz)\\,dx & =-\\int {x}^{2}dx \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{3x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nNow, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{3x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x}{C-{x}^{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition $y(1)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{3}{C-1}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3x}{(\\frac{5}{2}-{x}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x}{5-2{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17556/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e10cdc0-93c4-5b49-8eae-975665bb1d09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555/selection/2b699a4385c54cb845d7bd1e88a73e741f1f72a901d1a5d6f91422a86b977a23" :answer/id #uuid "1820de9d-ef31-56a9-8695-6e46c3923c24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555/selection/02d9a3b9768d50a977c946a7c34a9f8c45a9ceec950f7027ee14ee6b5d74cc7d" :answer/id #uuid "6720a05b-68b2-5303-a5ef-70861305e5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{2+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555/selection/3b45f798cc2d5300ec4414f663395e84066614922c35225d53fea76925f4f5e9" :answer/id #uuid "73789bd8-6291-56f1-9423-32ddde6e7fdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{1-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555/selection/59718787df3d3d529d389b2f9922ab425d0c42c94b4feac10ea923466f7f277a" :answer/id #uuid "060ea9af-82cd-5d9a-94c5-bfe3f2810194" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555/selection/dd30fb9493670647a0bfcdd6781909edad621907478e633e35ad7518548f9890" :answer/id #uuid "b69effbd-8ae4-5ced-9f78-230e2e8b692e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3-x}{1-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5d06905-1a8a-544b-b18c-7d994ef26210" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17555/selection/02d9a3b9768d50a977c946a7c34a9f8c45a9ceec950f7027ee14ee6b5d74cc7d" :answer-field/choices ["q-17555/selection/2b699a4385c54cb845d7bd1e88a73e741f1f72a901d1a5d6f91422a86b977a23" "q-17555/selection/02d9a3b9768d50a977c946a7c34a9f8c45a9ceec950f7027ee14ee6b5d74cc7d" "q-17555/selection/3b45f798cc2d5300ec4414f663395e84066614922c35225d53fea76925f4f5e9" "q-17555/selection/59718787df3d3d529d389b2f9922ab425d0c42c94b4feac10ea923466f7f277a" "q-17555/selection/dd30fb9493670647a0bfcdd6781909edad621907478e633e35ad7518548f9890"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17555" :question/id #uuid "1139c3ef-c69b-5554-a0ac-c343a4ed8799" :question/math-academy-id "q-17555" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{y(y-1)}{x}=0,\\,y(-1)=2,\\,x<0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation*\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}-\\frac{1}{x}z=-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\n*using the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}-\\frac{z}{x}=-\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x{|}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|x|} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x<0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=-\\frac{1}{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z) & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}z & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x}z) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x}z)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}z & =\\frac{1}{x}+C \\\\ z & =1+Cx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =1+Cx \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{1+Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition $y(-1)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{1-C}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{(1+\\frac{1}{2}x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2+x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17555/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e10cdc0-93c4-5b49-8eae-975665bb1d09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17555"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-17559"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y(y-1)}{x}=0,\\,y(1)=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =x+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{x+C}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{x+C}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition  $y(1)=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =\\frac{1}{1+C}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{(x-\\frac{4}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{(5x-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845/selection/0c345f9b02f71d1c29a614c3fe9c5196b92b385ecfad82a239a0233ee129d9f4" :answer/id #uuid "fd65bece-8622-57fc-b62d-f3fedd17815a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3+{e}^{-2x}}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845/selection/1936105aa0cc6a1e467fbca41436e5b78098cf2c935fdca1ca65e7393ad1fcd5" :answer/id #uuid "e6ff12e2-b78a-52ef-b5f6-92c5f643ad81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845/selection/914a49175aeb3b7e76d3f41f54f60445f7aad9f745a41584ff59b609faceadeb" :answer/id #uuid "abc91cf0-dc84-520d-aebe-855f904675d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1+3{e}^{x}}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845/selection/bac096650f9a44aeb31473eaa4507af1e3457f7dc355bb78813b0ab9e7cc663e" :answer/id #uuid "e676fed6-2eab-5f43-80f8-5cc2315c867b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{4-x}{\\sqrt{3}x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845/selection/00820c638bbeb69750e66f86fcdd712ea65680e873b829c089e44f08d97ccbf8" :answer/id #uuid "fae71869-d2d7-5aa0-8939-438aea71f06c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{5-2x}{\\sqrt{3}x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54a7c1bc-dbc4-5890-8841-a507278f57a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79845/selection/1936105aa0cc6a1e467fbca41436e5b78098cf2c935fdca1ca65e7393ad1fcd5" :answer-field/choices ["q-79845/selection/0c345f9b02f71d1c29a614c3fe9c5196b92b385ecfad82a239a0233ee129d9f4" "q-79845/selection/1936105aa0cc6a1e467fbca41436e5b78098cf2c935fdca1ca65e7393ad1fcd5" "q-79845/selection/914a49175aeb3b7e76d3f41f54f60445f7aad9f745a41584ff59b609faceadeb" "q-79845/selection/bac096650f9a44aeb31473eaa4507af1e3457f7dc355bb78813b0ab9e7cc663e" "q-79845/selection/00820c638bbeb69750e66f86fcdd712ea65680e873b829c089e44f08d97ccbf8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79845" :question/id #uuid "ec56e910-f89c-5f06-9e2f-0513c5da858e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79845" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+(x+1)y=\\frac{3}{xy},\\,y(1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,x>0,\\,y>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2z=6\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2z=6.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=2,\\,Q(x)=6\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2z) & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 6 \\\\ {e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2{e}^{2x}z & =6{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{2x}z) & =6{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{2x}z)\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{2x}z & =3{e}^{2x}+C \\\\ z & =3+C{e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{2} & =3+C{e}^{-2x} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{3+C{e}^{-2x}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+C{e}^{-2x}}}{x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $x>0$ and $y>0.$\n\nFrom the initial condition $y(1)=\\sqrt{3}$ we determine $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+C{e}^{-2}}}{1}\\,⟹\\,C=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79845/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e10cdc0-93c4-5b49-8eae-975665bb1d09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6867"] :question/problem "The substitution $z= y^2$ can be used to transform the equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} = \\dfrac{x+2}{2y} + 2x^2y\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form $z'(x) + P(x)z(x) = Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz= y^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 2y \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{2z^{1/2}}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2{z}^{1/2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+2}{2{z}^{1/2}}+2{x}^{2}{z}^{1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x).\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =x+2+4{x}^{2}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-4{x}^{2}z & =x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = - 4x^2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6606"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following first-order ODE using the substitution $z=y^3.$\n\n$$\nxy^2\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = x^2+y^3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's make a substitution\n\n$$\nz=y^3\\,.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}=3y^2\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\ny^2\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\n Consequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}\\right)=x^2+z\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3}{x}({x}^{2}+z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3x+\\frac{3}{x}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{3}{x}\\,z & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-\\frac{3}{x},\\,Q(x)=3x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-3/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x^3}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{3}{x}\\,z) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3x \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\,z & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{z}{{x}^{3}}) & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{z}{{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{z}{{x}^{3}} & =-\\frac{3}{x}+C \\\\ z & =-3{x}^{2}+C{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by substituting the solution into $z=y^3.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3} & =z \\\\ {y}^{3} & =-3{x}^{2}+C{x}^{3} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{-3{x}^{2}+C{x}^{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6605"] :question/problem "Find the specific solution of the first-order ODE\n\n$$\nxe^y\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}+e^y = e^{x} \\, ,\n$$\n\ngiven that $y(1)=1$ and $x>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's make a substitution\n\n$$\nz=e^y\\,.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ with the chain rule, we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}=e^y\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$ Consequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of  $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}+z=e^x\\,,\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition\n\n$$\nz(1)=e^{y(1)}=e^1=e\\,.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left-hand side of the differential equation is now an exact derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we determine the value of $C$ that satisfies the initial condition $z(1)=e\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z(1) & =e \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{1}+C}{1} & =e \\\\ e+C & =e \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have \n\n$$\nz  =   \\frac{e^x}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by substituting the solution into $z=e^y.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y} & =z \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x} \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x) \\\\  & =x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$ So, the final solution is\n\n$$\ny = x - \\ln (x), \\quad x > 0.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
